  "term": "hierarchical linear model",
  "definition": "A hierarchical linear model is a statistical approach used to study how factors from different levels, such as individual and school influences, relate to an outcome at the same time. It can also test whether a factor at one level changes the relationship between factors at another level and the outcome.",
